    "created_at": "2017-02-18T16:27:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-18T16:27:30Z",
    "body": "It seems @jyasskin did call out my feedback again but it got hidden due to the way GitHub deals with feedback. In particular I think the second argument should be a host too. I think that's what we want for cookies and what the underlying algorithm looks like in browsers, but it would be good if @mikewest could confirm before we made that change. (Anyone know of any other callers that are web-exposed (thus not browser UI)?)\r\n\r\n(And then I was also thinking of moving the algorithm to URL since that defines hosts, but maybe since HTML already defines the cookie API and `document.domain`, leaving the algorithm in HTML for now until we want to do more with it is actually fine.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/280856350/reactions",
